## 6. UX and Accessibility Requirements

**Navigation and orientation**
- Skip-to-content link as the first focusable element.
- Active section highlighting in the nav, and a thin scroll-progress line at the top of the page.
- Navbar hides on scroll down and shows on scroll up, so the content is not blocked.
- Every key page action is reachable in at most two clicks (`Get in touch` is in the nav and the hero, and anchors to Contact).
- The nav keeps `Get in touch` visible so a visitor returning from a portfolio tab still has a clear next step.

**External links (new tab)**
- Every link that opens a new tab uses `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Show a visible `↗` icon and add visually hidden text: "(opens in a new tab)".
- Use plain anchor tags, never `window.open()` (popup blockers can break it).
- Footer social links follow the same rules.
- The original page stays open, so no state is lost.

**Reduced motion** (`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`)
- Disable Lenis, pinning, parallax, scale effects and count-ups.
- Replace reveals with a simple 0.2s fade. Content must never depend on animation to be visible.

**Accessibility**
- Text over photos must meet WCAG AA contrast, so use a dark overlay of at least 40% on image sections.
- Visible focus states on all interactive elements.
- Descriptive alt text for every image, and `aria-hidden` for purely decorative ones.
- Drawer menu: focus trap, `Esc` closes it, and focus returns to the menu button.
- Hero video: muted, `playsInline`, no audio, with a pause control, and a still-image fallback.
- Headline line-splitting must keep the original text readable by screen readers (`aria-label` on the heading).

**Device and browser compatibility**
The design must work on every common device. No layout may depend on one specific screen.
- **Breakpoints (min-width):** 360 (small phones), 390 (primary mobile), 768 (tablet portrait), 1024 (tablet landscape / small laptop), 1440 (primary desktop), 1920+ (large desktop). Content max-width and image scaling must hold on large screens, with no stretched or pixelated imagery. Use fluid type (`clamp`) and relative units, not fixed-pixel layouts.
- **Orientation:** portrait and landscape both supported. On short landscape viewports (phones around 360–430px tall), `100svh` sections must not clip content: reduce headline size and padding with a `max-height` media query.
- **Input:** touch, mouse and keyboard all work. Hover is never required to reach content. Enable hover effects by capability, `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`, not by screen width, so tablets with keyboards or large touch screens behave correctly.
- **Smooth scroll:** Lenis only on fine-pointer devices. Touch devices use native scroll.
- **Browsers (last 2 major versions):** Chrome, Safari (iOS and macOS), Firefox, Edge, Samsung Internet. Safari checks: `100svh`, `clip-path`, `backdrop-filter` (include `-webkit-` prefix and a solid-color fallback), safe-area insets.
- **Zoom and text size:** layout survives 200% browser zoom and increased system text size with no horizontal scroll or overlapping text.
- **Test matrix before client sign-off:** small and large iPhone, mid-range Android phone, iPad (portrait and landscape), 13" laptop, 1920px desktop. Include a real-device check on iOS Safari and Android Chrome, because emulators do not show real scroll performance.

**Mobile**
- Pinning and heavy parallax are disabled below 1024px (phones and tablets in portrait), replaced by lightweight reveals.
- Tap targets are at least 44px. Container padding is 20px. Respect safe-area insets.
- Use `100svh`, never `100vh`.

**Performance budget**
- LCP under 2.5s, CLS under 0.1, and no jank while scrolling at 60fps on a mid-range phone.
- Hero image preloaded and served as AVIF or WebP with responsive `srcset`. All other images lazy-loaded.
- Every image has explicit width and height or an aspect-ratio box to avoid layout shift.
- Video is compressed, muted and short, with a poster image. It is not loaded on slow connections or when data-saver is on.
- Fonts: `font-display: swap`, subset to Latin, preloaded.
- Kill or refresh ScrollTrigger instances on unmount and on resize (`ScrollTrigger.refresh()` after images load).

